er-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558391}] :question/id #uuid "9b6fa50f-a6b0-54a4-b38d-0880cb666278" :question/math-academy-id "q-139656" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$2$** | **$4$** | **$6$** | **$8$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $13$ | $-4$ | $-18$ | $-10$ | $11$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$2$** | **$4$** | **$6$** | **$8$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $13$ | $-4$ | $-18$ | $-10$ | $11$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & {0}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 6 & {6}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 8 & {8}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558552 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05bb58d1-77b6-50fd-ab99-d2d4d323a0a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}15 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 9 \\\\ 7 & 14 \\\\ 3 & 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557881} {:answer/id #uuid "284566a0-3da3-